CASE
  AWPTCM-T20358 "Loopback between two ports on same switch", folder /xSTP/RSTP
  Objective: "When a switch port receives its own BPDU from the same edge port, it sets the port to the blocking
    state.
    When it no longer receives BPDUs, it sets the port to the forwarding state."
  Precondition: (empty)
  STEP 1 text:
    "- Connect the RSTP switch and a hub/switch.
     - Create a loop network switch.
     - Send broadcast traffic from IXIA
     - Confirm Port11 of RSTP switch. RSTP Port Role should be set to BackUp (Loopback Disabled) and State should
       set to Discarding.
     - Confirm backup port should not transmit traffic"
  STEP 1 expected: "Backup port should not forward any packet in this state."

BENCH MAPPING (dispatch ruling, queue row 1): the "loop" is the direct copper lead x230 port1.0.6 <-> port1.0.7
  (both AT-SPTX); "Port11" = x230 port1.0.7 (the higher port ID, 838f, so the one that becomes Backup); "IXIA" =
  tb470 eth3 (00:f0:4d:00:77:18, 10.38.215.65/27) <-> x230 port1.0.5. Everything in VLAN 105 (the isolation VLAN
  port1.0.5 already uses), so the loop and the broadcast stay in their own VLAN. Previous attempt 2026-10-09 was
  PARTIAL (no BPDU-transparent loop: the IE520 stack did not return BPDUs); the recable to the direct lead is what
  makes this run possible.

DEVICES: swi_f only (DUT, u0, AT-x230-28GS V2 S/N A10783G262900002, awplus_main-20261008-57, bridge ID
  8000:00c28f3f0f5d). No partner switch.
Configs saved: 20358/swi_f.cfg -- running-config at 11:25:36 after setup, before the loop was closed (so
