STEP 1 -- bullets 1-2: create the loop (x230 port1.0.6 <-> port1.0.7, same VLAN)
  First closure, 11:25:55-11:25:58 (header clock): `interface port1.0.7` / `no shutdown` / `end`, then the gate
    `@poll 20 port1\.0\.7\s+\S+\s+\S+\s+Backup\s+Discarding show spanning-tree brief`
    -> "@poll MATCHED after 5.1 s (3 reads) of 'show spanning-tree brief'"
       port1.0.6       8000:00c28f3f0f5d    838e       Designated       Forwarding
       port1.0.7       8000:00c28f3f0f5d    838f       Backup           Discarding
    The next command, `show spanning-tree interface port1.0.7`, prints every line prefixed `% ` on this build
    (e.g. "%   port1.0.7: Port Number 911 - Ifindex 5007 - Port Id 838f - Role Backup - State Discarding"), so
    ckcon --stop-on-error read it as a CLI error and stopped (rc 2). The safety branch then shut port1.0.7
    (emergency-shut.out, 11:26:12-11:26:16; device log 11:26:06 "port1.0.7 user shutdown"). That stop was the
    tool's reading of the `% ` prefix, not a device fault; the loop was already held by port1.0.7
    Backup/Discarding. Tool lesson: do not put `show spanning-tree interface` under --stop-on-error.
